# Share the project's editor settings and extension recommendations; keep
# personal launch configs and local overrides out.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ------------------------------------------------- large working-source files
#
# These two live in the repo root and are *not* build inputs — nothing in the
# app imports them, and the assets actually served are the derivatives already
# committed under `public/`:
#
#   OSPS Product List.xlsx  (18.6MB)  ->  public/downloads/osps-product-list.xlsx (47KB)
#   osps logo.pdf           ( 8.8MB)  ->  public/osps-*.webp, public/brand/*.png
#
# Together they are ~27MB, and anything committed to git stays in its history
# permanently even after a later delete. Uncomment the two lines below to keep
# them out — but only once they are backed up somewhere else, because they are
# the editable masters and the committed derivatives cannot be reversed into
# them. Leaving them commented (the default) tracks the files as normal.
#
# OSPS Product List.xlsx
# osps logo.pdf
